{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CegFD898USDomLxs25QCF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The verdict is committed at `73440151`. Review complete.\n\n**VERDICT: CHANGES-REQUESTED findings=4** — written to `docs/reviews/wi-579-the-verdict-carrier-and-the-ad/030-REVIEW-A-7880b99-relaxed.md`.\n\n## What I found\n\nThe headline is a **fail-open at the merge gate**, driven end-to-end rather than reasoned about:\n\n`kitlib/verdict.py:598` joins a round file to its coordinator session log by `(train, ordinal)` alone, and only checks that the log's phase is *a member of* `REVIEW_PHASES` — never that it *equals* the round file's own phase. So one logged REVIEW-A session's telemetry validates a `NNN-REVIEW-B-<sha>.md` written in the same commit. At `review_rounds = 2` the gate clears on a single reviewer, which is the entire content of policy 2.\n\nI drove it on the suite's own fixture: `logged_rounds` returned both phase files from one session log, `branch_entries` gave two APPROVEs, and `integrate._verdict_gate(...)` returned `None` — merge allowed. The `Review-Verdict` cross-check doesn't catch it either, because `round_count` is the max per-phase count and reads 1 either way.\n\nTwo things kept it at MAJOR rather than BLOCKER: the shipped default is `review_rounds = 1` in both this repo and the template, so it's latent here and bites the adopter who dials up.\n\nNotably, **LLR-207's Detail states the correct rule** — \"joins ... by train, ordinal and review phase\" — so the spine cell is right and the code under-implements it. That's finding 3, and it's the class where a row asserts a stronger binding than its module delivers with nothing detecting the gap.\n\nThe other two: WI-579 Done-when 3's scheduling half is genuinely uncovered (`schedule_adjudication_round` and `dispositions_drafted` appear under `tests/` only inside a ratchet *comment*), and the loop and gate look the branch spec up in **opposite precedence orders** — which weakens the \"one reader, so they cannot come apart\" claim at the drafts input. Plus a MINOR on `gen_verdict_rollup.train_dirs` silently producing nothing for the flat pre-train layout that `round_file` explicitly supports.\n\n## On the instruments\n\n`check.py --jobs 0` is **PASS** and `trace.py --strict-integrity` reports `integrity=0`. Both are quoted by summary in the verdict file. Worth flagging that neither instrument can see finding 1 — the harness is green *and* the gate is fail-open, because nothing in the check suite drives the cross-phase class.\n\nOne caveat on my own coverage claims: I did not run the full unfiltered suite, so Done-when 5's green is not re-driven here — I've recorded it as not verified rather than inherited from the spec's own account."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9887,"cache_read_input_tokens":148351,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9887},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3dc9afe5-1745-4be4-a0f8-62f60396f4a5","uuid":"d280eb4d-87a5-4114-b05d-8399ee1368ec","request_id":"req_011CegFD7HnFR5WgdNcWx2Yn"}
